{
  "id": "irhgpt5",
  "title": "CHAPTER 8 : SIMPLE INTEREST",
  "order": 11,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "n15wizv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FUNDAMENTAL CONCEPTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Simple Interest is calculated uniformly only on the initial principal amount throughout the entire period.",
        "The Principal (P) remains constant for the entire duration of the loan or investment.",
        "When time is given in months, it must be converted to years by dividing by 12 before applying the formula.",
        "The total Amount (A) at the end of the tenure is the sum of the Principal and Simple Interest."
      ],
      "id": "23vg228"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Core Formula",
          "value": "SI = (P×R×T)/100",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Total Amount",
          "value": "A = P + SI",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Time Standard",
          "value": "Years (T)",
          "icon": "clock"
        },
        {
          "label": "Target Exams",
          "value": "RRB & SSC",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "ckez7tw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lk1lpsa",
      "content": "Principal (P): The original sum of money that is borrowed or invested. Rate of Interest (R): The percentage charged on the principal per year."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wxxqvqe",
      "content": "Time (T): The duration for which the money is invested or borrowed. Time must always be expressed in years unless stated otherwise."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dxqpf80",
      "content": "Simple Interest (SI): The extra amount paid by the borrower or earned by the investor for using the money."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p6rbhay",
      "content": "Amount (A): The total money received at the end of the time period. Relationship: Amount = Principal + Simple Interest"
    },
    {
      "id": "on7srou",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MOST IMPORTANT FORMULAS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "npdcqk6",
      "content": "Simple Interest: SI = (P × R × T) / 100 Amount: A = P + SI"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ybg32tc",
      "content": "Direct Formula for Amount: A = P(1 + RT/100) Finding Principal: P = (SI × 100) / (R × T) Finding Rate: R = (SI × 100) / (P × T)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v4n7za5",
      "content": "Finding Time: T = (SI × 100) / (P × R)"
    },
    {
      "id": "qfc03t0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "VERY IMPORTANT EXAM INSIGHTS"
    },
    {
      "id": "1mkj3kh",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>If the principal is constant, simple interest increases uniformly every year.</li><li>The interest earned each year is always the same in Simple Interest.</li><li>SI is directly proportional to Principal, Rate, and Time.</li><li>Always convert months into years.</li></ul>",
        "If the principal is constant, simple interest increases uniformly every year.",
        "The interest earned each year is always the same in Simple Interest.",
        "SI is directly proportional to Principal, Rate, and Time.",
        "Always convert months into years."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cqn6sog",
      "content": "Example: 6 months = 1/2 year, 9 months = 3/4 year."
    },
    {
      "id": "d59lsp9",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>For days: Time = Number of days / 365 (generally used in advanced questions).</li></ul>",
        "For days: Time = Number of days / 365 (generally used in advanced questions)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4dglzgz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "POWER SHORTCUT (FREQUENT RRB MODEL)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dhce9j7",
      "content": "If the interest for 1 year is known, multiply it directly by the number of years. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iliz0q5",
      "content": "If interest on ₹2000 at 5% is ₹100 per year, then in 4 years the interest will be ₹400. No need to apply the formula repeatedly."
    },
    {
      "id": "5xgclmp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ADVANCED MODEL – DIFFERENCE BETWEEN AMOUNTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g0eyjcw",
      "content": "When the difference between amounts for two different time periods is given, remember: Difference in Amount = Interest for the extra time."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iovzjyr",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a3zzlwh",
      "content": "The difference between the amounts for 5 years and 3 years is ₹400. Extra time = 2 years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7saji3p",
      "content": "Interest for 1 year = 400 ÷ 2 = ₹200."
    },
    {
      "id": "2m1c4sx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SOLVED EXAMPLES"
    },
    {
      "id": "bj5yr40",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 1: Basic Simple Interest"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yoz6eod",
      "content": "Find the simple interest on ₹6000 at 10% per annum for 3 years. Step 1: Write the formula."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "phb7h1w",
      "content": "SI = (P × R × T) / 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c583pyx",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute the values. SI = (6000 × 10 × 3) / 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4ib3eif",
      "content": "Step 3: Simplify carefully before multiplying. 6000 ÷ 100 = 60"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "puoore9",
      "content": "Step 4: 60 × 10 × 3 = 1800"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "al3gtxu",
      "content": "Final Answer: The simple interest is ₹1800."
    },
    {
      "id": "o6cvw89",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 2: Finding Amount"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u4lyg4a",
      "content": "A sum of ₹4500 is invested at 8% per annum for 2 years. Find the amount."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d1zwfmm",
      "content": "Step 1: Calculate SI."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v4p0tiq",
      "content": "SI = (4500 × 8 × 2) / 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a6oao2i",
      "content": "First simplify: 4500 ÷ 100 = 45"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xolnznk",
      "content": "Now multiply: 45 × 8 × 2 = 720 Step 2: Add SI to the principal. Amount = 4500 + 720 = ₹5220."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Simple Interest is calculated uniformly on the principal amount for the entire period of time.",
      "id": "lzpq13w"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0dm0fbc",
      "content": "Final Answer: The amount is ₹5220."
    },
    {
      "id": "hm4cfaw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 3: Finding Rate"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "11yjs44",
      "content": "A principal of ₹5000 earns ₹1500 as simple interest in 5 years. Find the rate."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tj6ktdb",
      "content": "Step 1: Use the rate formula. R = (SI × 100) / (P × T)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wmwxgcl",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute values."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "msp1ybj",
      "content": "R = (1500 × 100) / (5000 × 5)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hvopxpw",
      "content": "Step 3: Simplify."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mn6ggue",
      "content": "150000 ÷ 25000 = 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cdpet08",
      "content": "Final Answer: The rate of interest is 6% per annum."
    },
    {
      "id": "mvczeg1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 4: Finding Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "52a6f6n",
      "content": "In how many years will ₹4000 earn ₹800 at 5% simple interest?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rx3z8yc",
      "content": "Step 1: Apply the time formula. T = (SI × 100) / (P × R)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gncl03c",
      "content": "Step 2: T = (800 × 100) / (4000 × 5)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0qg4lny",
      "content": "Step 3: 80000 ÷ 20000 = 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3ff7ozj",
      "content": "Final Answer: The required time is 4 years."
    },
    {
      "id": "6jbqmf4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Example 5: Months-Based Question"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7qnnx75",
      "content": "Find the simple interest on ₹2400 at 12% per annum for 9 months."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sdrybm8",
      "content": "Step 1: Convert months into years. 9 months = 9/12 = 3/4 year."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Simple Interest (SI)",
        "Compound Interest (CI)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Principal Base",
          "Calculated only on the initial principal amount",
          "Calculated on principal plus accumulated interest"
        ],
        [
          "Yearly Growth",
          "Interest amount remains constant every year",
          "Interest amount increases progressively each year"
        ],
        [
          "Formula",
          "SI = (P × R × T) / 100",
          "CI = P × (1 + R/100)^T - P"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "btmc3h7"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d3ozezw",
      "content": "Step 2: Apply the formula. SI = (2400 × 12 × 3/4) / 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4wkzgi8",
      "content": "Step 3: Simplify."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "u4g0p32",
      "content": "12 × 3/4 = 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y68avae",
      "content": "So, SI = (2400 × 9) / 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "301gri4",
      "content": "= 216"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xk9ik7f",
      "content": "Final Answer: The simple interest is ₹216."
    },
    {
      "id": "kdzbkbu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PRACTICE QUESTIONS WITH ULTRA-DETAILED SOLUTIONS"
    },
    {
      "id": "v3wwqke",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gvo2adi",
      "content": "Find the simple interest on ₹3200 at 5% per annum for 4 years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gzji2xd",
      "content": "SI = (3200 × 5 × 4) / 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u4lyrud",
      "content": "Simplify: 3200 ÷ 100 = 32"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0swhkxf",
      "content": "Now multiply: 32 × 5 × 4 = 640 Final Answer: ₹640."
    },
    {
      "id": "53u3b82",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6nja5b5",
      "content": "Find the principal if the interest is ₹540 at 9% for 2 years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dcc7e4f",
      "content": "P = (SI × 100) / (R × T) P = (540 × 100) / (9 × 2)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ylix4jf",
      "content": "= 54000 / 18"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "467nb7l",
      "content": "= 3000"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k7jv5t4",
      "content": "Final Answer: The principal is ₹3000."
    },
    {
      "id": "lj4wg3g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mo61k4p",
      "content": "What will be the amount on ₹7000 at 6% for 3 years?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dk4fklt",
      "content": "Step 1: Calculate SI."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3y196tc",
      "content": "SI = (7000 × 6 × 3) / 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zv60u6u",
      "content": "7000 ÷ 100 = 70"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Always ensure time (T) is in years: convert months by dividing by 12, and days by dividing by 365.",
        "In 'Sum becomes N times' questions, the Simple Interest earned is equal to (N - 1) × Principal.",
        "For questions involving the difference between amounts over two different time periods, calculate interest per year by subtracting the two amounts."
      ],
      "id": "kigyppw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sa3wtxa",
      "content": "70 × 6 × 3 = 1260"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9ll88wv",
      "content": "Step 2:Amount = 7000 + 1260 = ₹8260. Final Answer: ₹8260."
    },
    {
      "id": "8s977wp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ryvkq7z",
      "content": "The difference between the simple interests for 6 years and 4 years is ₹500. Find the yearly interest."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fga0ues",
      "content": "Extra time = 2 years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "emscrtk",
      "content": "Interest per year = 500 ÷ 2 = ₹250. Final Answer: Yearly interest is ₹250."
    },
    {
      "id": "7lhoerm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Question 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rw1djt3",
      "content": "Find the rate if ₹2000 becomes ₹2600 in 5 years at simple interest."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vgbpe0j",
      "content": "Step 1: Find SI."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nytwriy",
      "content": "SI = 2600 − 2000 = 600"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u02ub2k",
      "content": "Step 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "osctce0",
      "content": "R = (600 × 100) / (2000 × 5)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ps4jtzl",
      "content": "= 60000 / 10000"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qpwh6mt",
      "content": "= 6%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5o2y4z2",
      "content": "Final Answer: The rate is 6% per annum."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}